// Vitest Snapshot v1, https://vitest.dev/guide/snapshot.html

exports[`--version and --help > prints the short, example-led help 1`] = `
"intent-gateway: the gateway between your agent and Intent Cloud.

Try it now, with no setup (demo Intent Cloud on this machine, test keys, nothing can be bought):
  intent demo

Connect an agent:
  claude mcp add intent -- intent demo     the demo
  claude mcp add intent -- intent --trust-keys <file>

Commands:
  intent serve [--http]             MCP server over stdio (the default), or Streamable HTTP
  intent init [--yes]               first run: check the setup, offer Shop one-tap, print the connect line
  intent log                        each action: what it sent, what came back (-v, --json, --since 2h, --action, --last <n>, --follow, --utc)
  intent verify                     re-check the chain, receipts, approvals, this install (--skip-install-check: chain only)
  intent evidence <approval handle> one purchase's evidence pack (--out <file>); check it: verify --evidence <file>
  intent panel [--port <n>]         read-only local page: activity, purchases, approvals, policy, log, verify
  intent doctor                     check the setup; each problem comes with its fix
  intent pause                      stop every purchase not paid yet (then: status shows it; resume, after your passkey resume)
  intent policy show                the active policy and its policy.lock
  intent policy add <name> [--yes]  narrow the policy with a library policy (shows the diff first)
  intent policy test <cases.yaml>   run test cases against the active policy
  intent approver list              approver pins and flagged passkeys
  intent approver accept            make a flagged passkey the approver (at a terminal)
  intent wallet status              whether a Shop wallet is linked and its vault opens (--wait-budget: until agent payments are on)
  intent wallet link|unlink shop    link your Shop account (from an agent's shell: --start, then --finish), or revoke and delete it
  intent wallet check shop          Shop orders that no purchase in the log names (--since 7d)
  intent demo [--http]              run against a local demo Intent Cloud (HTTP when typed in a terminal)

Options for every command (and --help, --version):
  --demo               use the demo Intent Cloud and the demo data dir (<data dir>/demo)
  --trust-keys <file>  root keys for the Intent Cloud host: {"rootKeys":[{"kid":…,"jwk":…}]}

With no policy file the bundled zip-only policy applies: the only detail about you it sends is your ZIP code.
intent policy add per-order-60 (or another library policy) narrows it, here to $60 a cart.

Settings: INTENT_DATA_DIR, INTENT_POLICY, INTENT_CLOUD_URL, INTENT_HTTP_HOST, INTENT_HTTP_PORT,
INTENT_HTTP_TOKEN, INTENT_DEMO=1, INTENT_DEMO_CONFIRM_PORT (demo confirm page, default 8788),
INTENT_DEBUG=1 (stack traces), INTENT_WALLET_KEY_FILE (wallet key), INTENT_SHOP_CLIENT_ID (a Shop client other than the gateway's own).
"
`;
